{"name":"Asian Jute","hex":"#d4b78f","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"jute","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The coarse, strong fibre of the East Indian plants, Corchorus olitorius and Corchorus capsularis, used to make mats, paper, gunny cloth etc.","The plants from which this fibre is obtained."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jute"}],"entries":[{"title":"Jute","blocks":[{"text":"Jute is a long, rough, shiny bast fibre that can be spun into coarse, strong threads. It is produced from flowering plants in the genus Corchorus, of the mallow family Malvaceae. The primary source of the fiber is Corchorus olitorius, but such fiber is considered inferior to that derived from Corchorus capsularis."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Jute_-_Kolkata_2003-10-31_00538.JPG/330px-Jute_-_Kolkata_2003-10-31_00538.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jute","wikidata":"Q107211"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Jute_Field_Bangladesh_%287749587518%29.jpg/500px-Jute_Field_Bangladesh_%287749587518%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Jute_Field_Bangladesh_%287749587518%29.jpg/500px-Jute_Field_Bangladesh_%287749587518%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A jute field in Bangladesh","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJute_Field_Bangladesh_(7749587518).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Jute_Rope_%28%E0%AE%9A%E0%AE%A3%E0%AE%B2%E0%AF%8D_%E0%AE%95%E0%AE%AF%E0%AE%BF%E0%AE%B1%E0%AF%81%29.jpg/500px-Jute_Rope_%28%E0%AE%9A%E0%AE%A3%E0%AE%B2%E0%AF%8D_%E0%AE%95%E0%AE%AF%E0%AE%BF%E0%AE%B1%E0%AF%81%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wi